1
00:01:27,800 --> 00:01:31,480
<i>He never used to care about anyone.</i>
<i>But after meeting this cop,</i>

2
00:01:31,560 --> 00:01:32,960
it's like he's under a spell.

3
00:01:33,040 --> 00:01:34,520
Why doesn't Oab just take Peng out?

4
00:01:34,600 --> 00:01:36,680
If he's going after Peng,
he has to think carefully.

5
00:01:36,760 --> 00:01:38,240
He only gets one chance.

6
00:01:40,120 --> 00:01:41,760
What are you doing with my supplier?

7
00:01:48,520 --> 00:01:49,760
Watch out, Bro!

8
00:01:55,320 --> 00:01:58,120
What happened today
should clear your doubts about Dom.

9
00:02:00,280 --> 00:02:02,200
I couldn't find you in the ER. I thought…

10
00:02:05,040 --> 00:02:06,840
Since we can't cancel the mission,

11
00:02:06,920 --> 00:02:09,560
let me go in.
I'll finish it as quickly as possible.

12
00:02:09,639 --> 00:02:10,639
Is the chief okay with that?

13
00:02:10,720 --> 00:02:12,720
I'm joining this case too.

14
00:02:12,800 --> 00:02:15,760
A police station
called Oab in for questioning.

15
00:02:17,760 --> 00:02:21,120
Yes. I'll go in this afternoon.

16
00:02:21,200 --> 00:02:22,080
Yes.

17
00:02:23,920 --> 00:02:25,520
They must've taken their money.

18
00:02:25,600 --> 00:02:28,320
Either way, I have to go in
and explain what really happened.

19
00:02:28,920 --> 00:02:30,200
Wait.

20
00:02:30,280 --> 00:02:33,000
But what if they use money
to rewrite the truth?

21
00:02:34,640 --> 00:02:36,720
We may not have as much money as Peng.

22
00:02:38,640 --> 00:02:41,960
But we should have enough
to make sure the truth stays the truth.

23
00:02:44,120 --> 00:02:45,840
I called you in because it's my duty,

24
00:02:45,920 --> 00:02:48,000
so you can explain your side of the story.

25
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:52,040
Someone from their side started it.

26
00:02:52,120 --> 00:02:54,600
My people were only waiting
for the liquor supplier.

27
00:02:54,680 --> 00:02:55,720
Yes.

28
00:02:55,800 --> 00:02:58,160
I was waiting for the supplier
to get his contact number.

29
00:02:59,600 --> 00:03:01,280
But the owner

30
00:03:01,360 --> 00:03:03,440
said you brought people
to shut down his shop.

31
00:03:17,960 --> 00:03:19,400
Consider this

32
00:03:19,480 --> 00:03:22,520
an apology from us,
for causing you trouble.

33
00:03:39,880 --> 00:03:43,040
Well, let's just say
I'm giving you a warning this time.

34
00:03:43,120 --> 00:03:45,360
Yes.

35
00:03:45,960 --> 00:03:47,560
Thank you.

36
00:04:04,400 --> 00:04:07,200
Nothing is louder than money, Bro.

37
00:04:07,280 --> 00:04:10,920
Pfft. One stack of cash,
and it's just a warning.

38
00:04:11,920 --> 00:04:13,280
Are you doing anything tonight?

39
00:04:13,960 --> 00:04:15,120
I've got plans.

40
00:04:15,760 --> 00:04:17,480
Go ahead. I can go home myself.

41
00:04:18,079 --> 00:04:19,800
I'm gonna visit the guys
at the hospital too.

42
00:04:19,880 --> 00:04:22,680
Hey, I'm coming with you.
I want to visit Dom and Haw.

43
00:04:24,160 --> 00:04:25,000
Let's go separately.

44
00:04:25,720 --> 00:04:27,200
I have something to do.

45
00:04:28,480 --> 00:04:30,560
Something to do?

46
00:04:36,600 --> 00:04:37,640
Alright.

47
00:04:41,120 --> 00:04:43,400
Fon, wanna go get something to eat?

48
00:04:45,400 --> 00:04:48,600
I ate a lot of snacks today.
I don't think I can eat dinner.

49
00:04:48,680 --> 00:04:51,320
Oh, then maybe another day.

50
00:04:52,520 --> 00:04:53,360
Sorry about that.

51
00:04:54,280 --> 00:04:57,520
How about tomorrow? I'll treat you.

52
00:04:57,600 --> 00:04:59,840
Okay. You said it.

53
00:05:01,040 --> 00:05:02,160
Then I'll get going.

54
00:05:02,240 --> 00:05:03,240
- See you.
- Bye.

55
00:05:15,800 --> 00:05:17,040
Are you going to see Dom tonight?

56
00:05:38,120 --> 00:05:40,320
- Why are you here?
- I came to pick you up.

57
00:05:41,760 --> 00:05:43,840
- Where are we going?
- To visit Dom.

58
00:05:47,240 --> 00:05:48,960
You know Dom, right?

59
00:05:51,160 --> 00:05:51,800
Let's go.

60
00:06:03,080 --> 00:06:05,960
So you skipped dinner for a date?
Single people like me

61
00:06:06,040 --> 00:06:08,080
just have to keep eating alone, I guess.

62
00:06:10,280 --> 00:06:11,440
What are you complaining about?

63
00:06:12,560 --> 00:06:13,520
Ugh.

64
00:06:13,600 --> 00:06:15,320
I'm just complaining about the weather.

65
00:06:16,760 --> 00:06:19,080
Why complain? It's not even raining.

66
00:06:20,480 --> 00:06:22,720
I'm complaining
because the rain doesn't fall everywhere.

67
00:06:40,360 --> 00:06:41,320
How did you get here?

68
00:06:46,400 --> 00:06:47,240
Oab.

69
00:06:50,600 --> 00:06:52,320
Did you come with him?

70
00:06:57,440 --> 00:06:59,760
How are you? Feeling better?

71
00:07:00,360 --> 00:07:01,320
Well…

72
00:07:02,120 --> 00:07:04,000
I was thinking of going home today.

73
00:07:05,800 --> 00:07:07,200
Wait until you're better before you leave.

74
00:07:07,280 --> 00:07:10,960
Yeah. If anything happens,
at least you'll be near a doctor.

75
00:07:22,440 --> 00:07:25,480
I think I'll go get a knife
to cut some fruit.

76
00:07:48,920 --> 00:07:50,320
You seem different, Bro.

77
00:07:51,240 --> 00:07:52,240
How so?

78
00:07:54,440 --> 00:07:57,000
I don't know.
You've been smiling more than usual.

79
00:08:01,160 --> 00:08:04,200
I guess I'm happy.

80
00:08:31,080 --> 00:08:33,280
I forgot my bag.

81
00:08:33,360 --> 00:08:34,240
I'll go get it for you.

82
00:08:34,320 --> 00:08:36,840
It's okay. I'll get it myself.

83
00:08:37,360 --> 00:08:38,480
You should go ahead.

84
00:08:54,760 --> 00:08:55,760
Dom.

85
00:08:58,120 --> 00:08:59,960
I don't have feelings for him.

86
00:09:00,040 --> 00:09:01,800
But Oab might have feelings for you.

87
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:04,160
Dom.

88
00:09:11,200 --> 00:09:14,160
I know. I trust you.

89
00:09:19,960 --> 00:09:21,280
Dom.

90
00:09:34,920 --> 00:09:37,800
Oab, I told you not to wait.

91
00:09:39,240 --> 00:09:40,440
I changed my mind.

92
00:09:41,760 --> 00:09:43,640
I'd like to take you out for dinner.

93
00:09:50,080 --> 00:09:50,920
Shall we go?

94
00:10:32,520 --> 00:10:33,640
What's up?

95
00:10:33,720 --> 00:10:36,320
They're meeting at Star Garden
to talk about the land.

96
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:38,720
You're sure it's that land?

97
00:10:39,840 --> 00:10:41,080
Yes.

98
00:11:03,520 --> 00:11:04,680
Hello.

99
00:11:04,760 --> 00:11:06,960
- The usual, two servings.
- Sure. This way, please.

100
00:11:07,640 --> 00:11:09,040
Let's go.

101
00:11:14,080 --> 00:11:16,280
- Right this way.
- Thank you.

102
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:21,920
When you eat out at night,

103
00:11:23,080 --> 00:11:24,440
you have to be a little careful.

104
00:11:24,520 --> 00:11:27,200
So that's why we're sitting
in the kitchen like this?

105
00:11:27,800 --> 00:11:30,120
Special place for a special person.

106
00:11:31,760 --> 00:11:32,920
Hey.

107
00:11:33,000 --> 00:11:35,000
This is Fon. Fon, this is

108
00:11:35,080 --> 00:11:36,520
Tee, my friend.

109
00:11:43,600 --> 00:11:44,640
Thank you.

110
00:11:46,560 --> 00:11:49,120
You're the first woman

111
00:11:49,200 --> 00:11:50,640
Oab has ever brought here.

112
00:11:51,880 --> 00:11:53,760
- Hey, two servings, right?
- Two.

113
00:11:53,840 --> 00:11:54,880
I'll get it ready.

114
00:11:58,240 --> 00:11:59,880
I met Tee

115
00:11:59,960 --> 00:12:01,760
when I first started working.

116
00:12:08,520 --> 00:12:10,920
With this many people,
will I even get work?

117
00:12:11,000 --> 00:12:12,480
Just wait your turn.

118
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:16,720
The other day, someone cut the line
and got beaten badly.

119
00:12:21,480 --> 00:12:23,120
Things like this require guts.

120
00:12:23,200 --> 00:12:24,800
- Hey, it's here.
- Oab!

121
00:12:24,880 --> 00:12:25,880
- Hey, Oab!
- The truck's here.

122
00:12:25,960 --> 00:12:27,360
Pong, come on.

123
00:12:28,160 --> 00:12:29,360
- Let's go, Pong.
- Hey.

124
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:30,960
Get in line.

125
00:12:31,680 --> 00:12:32,640
No.

126
00:12:33,600 --> 00:12:35,160
- What's going on?
- You started this.

127
00:12:48,560 --> 00:12:51,240
We fought a few times,
and that's how we got close.

128
00:12:51,840 --> 00:12:53,520
After that,
we started taking jobs together.

129
00:12:54,560 --> 00:12:55,400
Thank you.

130
00:12:55,480 --> 00:12:57,360
Life was damn hard back then.

131
00:12:57,440 --> 00:12:59,960
But it was so much fun. Right, Oab?

132
00:13:00,040 --> 00:13:01,040
Yeah, it was.

133
00:13:01,800 --> 00:13:03,840
Boss, five pork noodles with gravy.

134
00:13:03,920 --> 00:13:05,040
Yeah, got it.

135
00:13:11,800 --> 00:13:14,960
We worked as day laborers for so long
before we finally got a contract.

136
00:13:21,760 --> 00:13:22,880
Fon.

137
00:13:24,600 --> 00:13:27,080
I never forgot the promise I made to you.

138
00:13:30,040 --> 00:13:33,120
I just wasn't ready yet.

139
00:13:38,160 --> 00:13:39,960
How did you go from being a contractor

140
00:13:40,040 --> 00:13:42,920
to becoming a powerful figure?

141
00:13:48,800 --> 00:13:52,320
I never wanted to be one, Fon.
I never wanted influence.

142
00:13:53,560 --> 00:13:57,200
I just wanted to build a business
that could give me stability,

143
00:13:58,840 --> 00:14:00,400
and come back to you.

144
00:14:02,800 --> 00:14:03,760
That's all.

145
00:14:04,960 --> 00:14:07,720
But society forced me
into becoming someone with power.

146
00:14:07,800 --> 00:14:09,880
Otherwise,
people would've taken advantage of me,

147
00:14:10,640 --> 00:14:14,400
and I wouldn't have survived.
If we don't fight back, they will.

148
00:14:18,600 --> 00:14:21,760
But there are
plenty of people without power

149
00:14:21,840 --> 00:14:23,160
whose businesses still survive.

150
00:14:27,120 --> 00:14:30,960
What do you mean by power
when you say that?

151
00:14:35,720 --> 00:14:36,640
Well…

152
00:14:36,720 --> 00:14:39,600
Having money, authority,

153
00:14:39,680 --> 00:14:43,320
connections, and being above the law.

154
00:14:44,640 --> 00:14:45,800
Well…

155
00:14:51,000 --> 00:14:53,840
Arm died because I refused to give in
to powerful people.

156
00:14:56,200 --> 00:14:58,920
Even now, the person who did it
still hasn't been caught, Fon.

157
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:00,960
How much do you think
the law has helped me?

158
00:15:05,760 --> 00:15:08,720
If I really had power above the law
like you say,

159
00:15:12,120 --> 00:15:14,600
the person who did it
wouldn't be living happily like this.

160
00:15:18,320 --> 00:15:20,160
You know who did it?

161
00:15:20,240 --> 00:15:21,200
I do.

162
00:15:22,360 --> 00:15:23,480
Can you tell me?

163
00:15:31,440 --> 00:15:32,720
Peng.

164
00:15:34,760 --> 00:15:36,320
Pichet Surangkul?

165
00:15:37,840 --> 00:15:38,760
But…

166
00:15:38,840 --> 00:15:40,800
He's famous.

167
00:15:40,880 --> 00:15:43,040
He owns real estate businesses

168
00:15:43,120 --> 00:15:45,840
and a lot of major entertainment venues.

169
00:15:47,640 --> 00:15:49,440
You may see me

170
00:15:49,520 --> 00:15:52,280
as a powerful person.
But the business I'm in requires me

171
00:15:53,640 --> 00:15:54,960
to rely on other people.

172
00:15:55,680 --> 00:15:58,680
My competitors don't just have money.
They have connections and power.

173
00:15:58,760 --> 00:16:00,360
They have people backing them.

174
00:16:01,480 --> 00:16:03,240
If I stood alone, I wouldn't survive.

175
00:16:04,200 --> 00:16:05,120
Some people really are

176
00:16:05,200 --> 00:16:08,480
like you said, they're above the law.

177
00:16:09,760 --> 00:16:10,760
On my own,

178
00:16:12,360 --> 00:16:13,760
I wouldn't stand a chance.

179
00:16:13,840 --> 00:16:15,240
So…

180
00:16:16,960 --> 00:16:18,640
Do you ever think about quitting?

181
00:16:27,400 --> 00:16:28,480
I do.

182
00:16:37,440 --> 00:16:39,280
But first, I have to avenge Arm.

183
00:16:42,200 --> 00:16:45,480
The person who did it
has to pay for what they did.

184
00:17:03,280 --> 00:17:05,319
Thank you for taking me out for dinner.

185
00:17:06,000 --> 00:17:08,599
I can take you out more often
if you don't mind.

186
00:17:13,040 --> 00:17:14,720
You can just drop me off here, Oab.

187
00:17:17,280 --> 00:17:20,599
Then I'll take you out
for dinner again sometime.

188
00:17:22,520 --> 00:17:23,880
Okay.

189
00:17:49,680 --> 00:17:51,880
You went to visit Dom
with that cop, right?

190
00:17:54,400 --> 00:17:55,760
Yeah.

191
00:17:57,000 --> 00:17:59,560
She's beautiful, but she's a cop.

192
00:18:01,400 --> 00:18:02,240
So what?

193
00:18:03,560 --> 00:18:05,280
I haven't done anything wrong.

194
00:18:06,880 --> 00:18:08,040
You haven't done anything wrong?

195
00:18:08,120 --> 00:18:09,880
Running a gambling den isn't wrong?

196
00:18:10,480 --> 00:18:12,320
Illegal lending isn't wrong?

197
00:18:13,040 --> 00:18:15,560
Sending your fighters to collect debts
isn't wrong either?

198
00:18:16,600 --> 00:18:17,400
Then I'm a little wrong.

199
00:18:19,600 --> 00:18:21,240
You need to get a grip, Oab.

200
00:18:21,320 --> 00:18:22,920
With Dom and the police,

201
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:25,800
you can't let your guard down like this.

202
00:18:32,480 --> 00:18:34,920
Listen carefully.
Don't get involved with those two.

203
00:18:35,960 --> 00:18:38,080
I know exactly what I'm doing.

204
00:18:45,880 --> 00:18:47,400
Why were you waiting for me?

205
00:18:54,000 --> 00:18:55,400
It's about the land you want.

206
00:18:57,320 --> 00:18:59,240
Peng wants it too.

207
00:19:02,520 --> 00:19:04,440
Then set up a meeting with the owner.

208
00:19:05,360 --> 00:19:06,920
I'll close the deal before they do.

209
00:19:16,440 --> 00:19:18,320
How much did they offer you?

210
00:19:19,600 --> 00:19:21,520
Exactly what I asked for.

211
00:19:28,720 --> 00:19:31,080
Then I'll give you one million more.

212
00:19:32,560 --> 00:19:33,560
Sell it to me.

213
00:19:35,720 --> 00:19:39,200
To keep things fair,
I'll let the other side

214
00:19:39,920 --> 00:19:41,560
know your offer first.

215
00:19:41,640 --> 00:19:43,160
Hey, Boss.

216
00:19:43,240 --> 00:19:44,960
You're just trying to drive up the price.

217
00:19:45,040 --> 00:19:47,920
We contacted you first,
and now he's offering another million.

218
00:19:48,000 --> 00:19:48,800
It's okay.

219
00:19:52,240 --> 00:19:55,240
Boss, I want this land.

220
00:19:57,360 --> 00:19:59,680
But I'm not stupid enough
to let you rip me off.

221
00:20:02,600 --> 00:20:06,080
Honestly, I could threaten you,
but I don't want to do that.

222
00:20:09,120 --> 00:20:10,320
Anyway,

223
00:20:11,000 --> 00:20:12,240
think it over.

224
00:20:13,360 --> 00:20:15,840
If you agree, set a time.

225
00:20:16,880 --> 00:20:19,080
I'll bring cash and pay you myself.

226
00:20:22,080 --> 00:20:22,920
Let's go.

227
00:20:57,720 --> 00:20:58,560
What are you looking into?

228
00:21:00,040 --> 00:21:01,360
Arm's case.

229
00:21:04,880 --> 00:21:06,280
Did Oab ask you to look into it?

230
00:21:06,880 --> 00:21:10,520
No. I'm just wondering
what really happened.

231
00:21:13,280 --> 00:21:14,560
What are you suspicious about?

232
00:21:15,720 --> 00:21:17,960
Ever since he was shot,
everything went quiet.

233
00:21:18,640 --> 00:21:22,360
The report says
the shooter fled to the border.

234
00:21:22,440 --> 00:21:24,520
But no one gave any information
about who hired him.

235
00:21:24,600 --> 00:21:26,440
There's nothing in the report

236
00:21:26,520 --> 00:21:29,240
about the person
who ordered the hit either.

237
00:21:29,840 --> 00:21:31,320
Then the case just went quiet,

238
00:21:31,400 --> 00:21:34,840
like it couldn't be closed,
and it disappeared.

239
00:21:36,880 --> 00:21:38,520
Maybe it just couldn't move forward.

240
00:21:53,000 --> 00:21:55,640
The boxer who was shot
after the match, right?

241
00:21:55,720 --> 00:21:56,680
Yeah.

242
00:21:57,360 --> 00:21:58,560
Why wasn't the case closed?

243
00:21:59,520 --> 00:22:01,440
They couldn't catch the shooter.

244
00:22:02,040 --> 00:22:04,320
Couldn't catch him, or didn't want to?

245
00:22:09,400 --> 00:22:10,560
Probably didn't want to.

246
00:22:13,640 --> 00:22:14,480
Hey.

247
00:22:15,280 --> 00:22:16,880
So there are no suspects,

248
00:22:17,400 --> 00:22:19,480
and no information about who hired him?

249
00:22:19,560 --> 00:22:21,360
What about Peng?

250
00:22:21,440 --> 00:22:23,600
The owner of Ocean Gym,
who lost that fight.

251
00:22:25,960 --> 00:22:26,720
Look.

252
00:22:27,320 --> 00:22:29,800
Some things are beyond people like us.

253
00:22:29,880 --> 00:22:33,440
We can suspect someone,
but if the investigators don't,

254
00:22:33,520 --> 00:22:35,160
what can we do?

255
00:22:41,760 --> 00:22:43,240
Harder!

256
00:22:45,560 --> 00:22:46,840
Dum.

257
00:22:46,920 --> 00:22:48,600
- Hello.
- Hello.

258
00:22:48,680 --> 00:22:51,160
You're back? Why didn't you tell me?
I would've picked you up.

259
00:22:51,240 --> 00:22:52,720
It's okay. I didn't want to bother you.

260
00:22:52,800 --> 00:22:53,960
How are you feeling?

261
00:22:54,560 --> 00:22:56,960
The doctor said
we can both go home and rest now.

262
00:22:58,480 --> 00:22:59,600
Are you sure you're okay?

263
00:23:01,080 --> 00:23:03,480
If we weren't okay,
they wouldn't have let us leave.

264
00:23:06,880 --> 00:23:08,360
He's fine, Bro.

265
00:23:09,520 --> 00:23:12,320
- But I'm not.
- Sit down slowly. It's okay.

266
00:23:12,840 --> 00:23:13,680
Dum.

267
00:23:14,280 --> 00:23:17,080
Can I take a few days off, if that's okay?

268
00:23:17,160 --> 00:23:19,720
Yeah, take a few days off.
Get better first.

269
00:23:19,800 --> 00:23:22,560
If you don't mind,
could you mop the floor for me?

270
00:23:22,640 --> 00:23:24,320
I'll take care of it. Don't worry.

271
00:23:24,400 --> 00:23:26,000
The boxing ring too.

272
00:23:26,080 --> 00:23:28,680
Mop the ring and wipe down the gloves too.

273
00:23:30,160 --> 00:23:32,120
- And don't forget the bathroom.
- Really?

274
00:23:32,200 --> 00:23:35,000
- Yes.
- That's enough.

275
00:23:35,080 --> 00:23:36,000
Huh?

276
00:23:36,080 --> 00:23:37,520
Bro, I'm injured!

277
00:23:40,280 --> 00:23:42,560
Dum, did you find a liquor supplier yet?

278
00:23:44,240 --> 00:23:48,480
Not yet. Oab and Pong
are trying to figure something out.

279
00:23:49,320 --> 00:23:52,120
How can the bar stay open
if it has no liquor to sell?

280
00:23:52,200 --> 00:23:53,320
If the bar doesn't open,

281
00:23:53,400 --> 00:23:54,840
you guys won't have work.

282
00:23:55,640 --> 00:23:58,440
If the bar doesn't open,
I won't be working at the bar anymore?

283
00:23:58,520 --> 00:23:59,520
Yeah.

284
00:24:01,800 --> 00:24:03,720
I'll talk to Oab.

285
00:24:03,800 --> 00:24:05,520
If the bar still can't open,

286
00:24:06,120 --> 00:24:07,880
I'll have you guys collect debts for now.

287
00:24:08,920 --> 00:24:11,760
But if that doesn't work out,
you'll be out of work.

288
00:24:16,280 --> 00:24:18,320
I'll go outside
after I finish packing up, okay?

289
00:24:18,400 --> 00:24:19,760
Do whatever you want.

290
00:24:23,040 --> 00:24:23,800
SUBMISSION
OF HOMICIDE INVESTIGATION REPORT

291
00:24:24,840 --> 00:24:25,600
CRIMINAL INVESTIGATION CASE FILE
POST-MORTEM EXAMINATION FILE

292
00:24:26,760 --> 00:24:27,760
CASE INVESTIGATOR

293
00:24:29,160 --> 00:24:30,960
Why are the investigators' names
blacked out?

294
00:24:40,920 --> 00:24:42,520
If Peng wants that land,

295
00:24:42,600 --> 00:24:44,760
the price
is going to get ridiculously high.

296
00:24:44,840 --> 00:24:46,200
Are you going to compete with him?

297
00:24:47,560 --> 00:24:48,680
I am.

298
00:24:49,840 --> 00:24:52,440
I've been wondering
if Peng can even afford it.

299
00:24:55,160 --> 00:24:56,640
If he's serious about getting it,

300
00:24:58,040 --> 00:24:59,040
shouldn't you find another place?

301
00:24:59,120 --> 00:24:59,960
No.

302
00:25:01,640 --> 00:25:04,160
This place is going to become
a major city someday.

303
00:25:04,920 --> 00:25:07,600
If I build a housing development there,
I'll make huge profits.

304
00:25:11,160 --> 00:25:12,000
What is it?

305
00:25:14,200 --> 00:25:15,840
Didn't you just get out of the hospital?

306
00:25:17,400 --> 00:25:19,000
How about supporting Thai liquor, Bro?

307
00:25:22,560 --> 00:25:26,200
Since no one will sell us imported liquor,
we'll sell Thai liquor ourselves.

308
00:25:26,280 --> 00:25:28,560
We'll become a distributor
and open our own shop.

309
00:25:28,640 --> 00:25:31,080
Becoming a distributor isn't that easy.

310
00:25:33,720 --> 00:25:36,280
But if you're okay
with this factory's deal,

311
00:25:36,360 --> 00:25:37,520
they're willing to work with us.

312
00:25:39,000 --> 00:25:40,280
How did you talk to them?

313
00:25:47,040 --> 00:25:49,040
I don't want to supply directly to bars.

314
00:25:49,680 --> 00:25:52,320
It would hurt my distributors' prices.

315
00:25:54,800 --> 00:25:57,720
What if my bar only sells your brand?

316
00:25:58,400 --> 00:25:59,920
When other places want to buy wholesale,

317
00:26:00,000 --> 00:26:01,880
I can supply them too,

318
00:26:01,960 --> 00:26:04,160
like I'm another one of your partners.

319
00:26:05,880 --> 00:26:08,240
Yeah, that's actually interesting.

320
00:26:10,720 --> 00:26:13,320
If you're interested, what documents

321
00:26:13,400 --> 00:26:14,680
do I need to submit?

322
00:26:16,440 --> 00:26:17,280
Here you go.

323
00:26:17,360 --> 00:26:19,960
SALES MANAGER

324
00:26:21,600 --> 00:26:23,840
This is
the factory manager's business card.

325
00:26:25,960 --> 00:26:29,200
How can Thai liquor
compete with imported liquor?

326
00:26:30,840 --> 00:26:32,280
It can.

327
00:26:32,360 --> 00:26:34,840
You just need good promotions,
good campaigns,

328
00:26:34,920 --> 00:26:37,360
and advertise
that it's been around for over 20 years.

329
00:26:38,000 --> 00:26:39,520
I think it'll work.

330
00:26:40,920 --> 00:26:42,840
Hey, I think the taste is pretty good.

331
00:26:42,920 --> 00:26:45,800
We should give it a try.
It's better than having no liquor to sell.

332
00:26:52,440 --> 00:26:54,640
Pong, handle the paperwork.

333
00:27:04,440 --> 00:27:05,880
- What do you want?
- Last night,

334
00:27:05,960 --> 00:27:06,880
he got knocked out in the third round.

335
00:27:06,960 --> 00:27:09,080
- It was insane.
- So exciting.

336
00:27:10,000 --> 00:27:11,280
- Ma'am.
- What?

337
00:27:11,360 --> 00:27:12,720
One red soda and one cola, please.

338
00:27:12,800 --> 00:27:14,760
One red soda and one cola.

339
00:27:18,800 --> 00:27:19,640
Wait, Ma'am.

340
00:27:20,320 --> 00:27:22,680
No red soda. Make it two colas instead.

341
00:27:22,760 --> 00:27:23,840
- No more red soda?
- Yeah.

342
00:27:23,920 --> 00:27:24,880
- Two colas.
- Yeah.

343
00:27:29,440 --> 00:27:30,480
Get me cold ones, okay?

344
00:27:33,520 --> 00:27:34,640
Geez.

345
00:27:34,720 --> 00:27:36,440
Cold? What time do you want them?

346
00:27:36,520 --> 00:27:38,600
It's already 5 p.m.

347
00:27:38,680 --> 00:27:40,040
Isn't that cold enough?

348
00:27:41,480 --> 00:27:43,000
Seriously, Ma'am? Was that a joke?

349
00:27:43,080 --> 00:27:45,760
I'm Suk, not some joke.
Are you buying or not?

350
00:27:46,400 --> 00:27:47,600
Ma'am.

351
00:27:47,680 --> 00:27:50,000
- What?
- Ma'am, he means

352
00:27:50,080 --> 00:27:51,480
two cold colas.

353
00:27:51,560 --> 00:27:55,520
Oh, okay. Say it like that!

354
00:27:55,600 --> 00:27:57,200
Order like him.

355
00:27:58,160 --> 00:27:59,480
She never talks to me like that.

356
00:27:59,560 --> 00:28:00,960
That's my business.

357
00:28:01,560 --> 00:28:03,560
I have double standards.

358
00:28:03,640 --> 00:28:05,680
I'll do whatever I want.

359
00:28:05,760 --> 00:28:07,520
- None of your business.
- She hears everything.

360
00:28:08,520 --> 00:28:09,640
- Thank you.
- Here you go.

361
00:28:09,720 --> 00:28:11,120
- Such a hassle.
- Dom.

362
00:28:12,320 --> 00:28:14,280
- Hey.
- Okay.

363
00:28:17,120 --> 00:28:18,040
Yes, Oab?

364
00:28:21,560 --> 00:28:25,000
That liquor idea of yours is good.

365
00:28:27,560 --> 00:28:30,120
I think it's good too.
At least you won't have to rely on

366
00:28:30,200 --> 00:28:31,800
those imported liquor suppliers anymore.

367
00:28:34,520 --> 00:28:36,640
But what if people want imported liquor?

368
00:28:36,720 --> 00:28:38,760
I still think Thai liquor is great.

369
00:28:38,840 --> 00:28:42,560
Maybe your regular customers
will give it a try. It's cheaper.

370
00:28:43,320 --> 00:28:46,840
If you run good promotions,
you might even get more customers.

371
00:28:51,200 --> 00:28:53,400
If the bar survives, I survive too.

372
00:29:15,720 --> 00:29:16,840
- Ma'am.
- What?

373
00:29:16,920 --> 00:29:18,360
One red soda and one cola, please.

374
00:29:18,440 --> 00:29:20,640
One red soda and one cola.

375
00:29:24,080 --> 00:29:26,280
COME MEET ME

376
00:29:37,400 --> 00:29:38,360
That's for table one.

377
00:29:38,440 --> 00:29:40,240
See you at the camp.
I've got something to do.

378
00:29:40,320 --> 00:29:41,880
Huh? Where are you going?

379
00:30:23,560 --> 00:30:24,760
What the hell is he doing here?

380
00:30:50,160 --> 00:30:51,200
Who the hell are you?

381
00:30:52,960 --> 00:30:54,000
What are you doing here?

382
00:30:54,080 --> 00:30:55,800
- Pong!
- What are you doing here?

383
00:30:56,400 --> 00:30:57,560
Put the gun down.

384
00:30:57,640 --> 00:31:00,520
I should be the one asking who you are
and why you're here.

385
00:31:04,800 --> 00:31:08,320
Hey! Are you two cops?

386
00:31:15,560 --> 00:31:16,640
You're not cops?

387
00:31:18,200 --> 00:31:19,480
I'm here to buy a gun.

388
00:31:30,040 --> 00:31:31,760
I thought you were meeting the cops.

389
00:31:33,040 --> 00:31:35,560
Come on, Bro. You still don't trust me?

390
00:31:36,160 --> 00:31:37,320
Of course not.

391
00:31:38,600 --> 00:31:41,640
Who would've thought
you'd buy an illegal gun?

392
00:31:43,400 --> 00:31:45,640
Pong, I almost died the other day.

393
00:31:46,280 --> 00:31:48,160
I need something to protect myself.

394
00:31:48,240 --> 00:31:49,720
That's how it is.

395
00:31:52,200 --> 00:31:53,760
Better to have one on you.

396
00:32:14,400 --> 00:32:17,160
I'm not taking you back.
I've got something to do.

397
00:32:18,280 --> 00:32:20,240
Let me handle it for you next time.

398
00:32:21,600 --> 00:32:22,520
You can't do it.

399
00:32:23,440 --> 00:32:25,680
Hey, just tell me what to do.
I can handle it.

400
00:32:27,360 --> 00:32:28,680
You're no match for Peng's guys.

401
00:32:30,240 --> 00:32:31,560
You'll just get yourself killed.

402
00:33:08,000 --> 00:33:08,880
What took you so long?

403
00:33:14,560 --> 00:33:15,400
Who are you?

404
00:33:15,480 --> 00:33:16,680
Chief Saen sent me.

405
00:33:19,440 --> 00:33:21,280
I'm responsible for you
during this operation.

406
00:33:37,080 --> 00:33:39,920
Good thing Chief Saen told me to go there
if I was followed.

407
00:33:53,000 --> 00:33:54,000
I was followed.

408
00:34:05,840 --> 00:34:07,440
Good thing you realized it in time.

409
00:34:07,520 --> 00:34:11,120
I called you here
because Chief Saen wanted me to tell you

410
00:34:12,400 --> 00:34:14,159
that Fon has requested to join this case.

411
00:34:18,840 --> 00:34:20,760
Don't blow your cover.

412
00:34:20,840 --> 00:34:23,920
Don't let Oab find out
that you and Fon are a couple.

413
00:34:52,960 --> 00:34:54,280
<i>You seem different, Bro.</i>

414
00:34:54,360 --> 00:34:57,240
<i>- You've been smiling more than usual.</i>
<i>- I guess I'm happy.</i>

415
00:35:00,840 --> 00:35:02,400
<i>Do you know him?</i>

416
00:35:02,480 --> 00:35:03,760
Oab?

417
00:35:04,400 --> 00:35:06,000
<i>I don't have feelings for him.</i>

418
00:35:06,080 --> 00:35:07,840
But Oab might have feelings for you.

419
00:35:36,120 --> 00:35:36,960
Dom.

420
00:35:41,640 --> 00:35:42,880
How did you get here?

421
00:35:42,960 --> 00:35:44,440
Does anyone know you came?

422
00:35:46,840 --> 00:35:47,840
Worried Oab will find out?

423
00:35:50,000 --> 00:35:51,160
Yes.

424
00:35:53,440 --> 00:35:55,360
You requested
a transfer to my case, right?

425
00:35:57,160 --> 00:35:58,640
When were you going to tell me?

426
00:36:06,520 --> 00:36:08,680
I was going to tell you at the hospital.

427
00:36:09,640 --> 00:36:11,440
But I couldn't find the right moment.

428
00:36:16,200 --> 00:36:18,000
Why did you want to work on this case?

429
00:36:22,000 --> 00:36:23,120
Because of you.

430
00:36:24,200 --> 00:36:25,280
Are you sure?

431
00:36:26,360 --> 00:36:28,480
Are you sure that's the only reason?

432
00:36:29,320 --> 00:36:32,280
If it's not because of you,
then why do you think I did it?

433
00:36:33,040 --> 00:36:34,040
Because of Oab.

434
00:36:35,280 --> 00:36:37,920
I thought
you'd be better off with him than me.

435
00:36:39,240 --> 00:36:40,240
Don't be stupid, Dom.

436
00:36:40,840 --> 00:36:42,120
Then explain it to me.

437
00:36:44,480 --> 00:36:47,080
The day you were taken to the hospital,
covered in blood,

438
00:36:47,160 --> 00:36:49,080
how do you think a wife would feel?

439
00:36:49,160 --> 00:36:51,520
Her husband could die,
and she could do nothing but watch.

440
00:36:51,600 --> 00:36:53,440
She couldn't even show
that she was worried.

441
00:36:54,320 --> 00:36:55,880
Do you think that's okay?

442
00:36:56,760 --> 00:37:00,520
If you were in my place,
would you let me risk my life like that?

443
00:37:03,920 --> 00:37:05,840
- No.
- Exactly.

444
00:37:06,840 --> 00:37:08,640
I don't want to become a widow,

445
00:37:09,560 --> 00:37:12,480
and I don't want you risking your life
while I can do nothing.

446
00:37:13,960 --> 00:37:15,480
Then what can you do?

447
00:37:17,640 --> 00:37:18,880
I don't know.

448
00:37:19,600 --> 00:37:21,800
But at least I can stay close to you,

449
00:37:21,880 --> 00:37:23,840
know what you're doing,

450
00:37:23,920 --> 00:37:25,960
and help if I can.

451
00:37:39,600 --> 00:37:41,040
You weren't expecting anyone, right?

452
00:37:55,000 --> 00:37:56,080
Oab is here.

453
00:38:22,840 --> 00:38:26,040
I called you earlier,
but you didn't answer.

454
00:38:30,200 --> 00:38:31,520
<i>Can I get your number?</i>

455
00:38:39,320 --> 00:38:40,440
Give me your hand.

456
00:38:48,800 --> 00:38:50,000
You wanted my number, right?

457
00:38:57,760 --> 00:38:59,440
I was going to leave, but then

458
00:38:59,520 --> 00:39:02,320
I saw someone downstairs.
I asked if he knew your room.

459
00:39:03,280 --> 00:39:06,720
He gave me your room number,
so I came up to check.

460
00:39:10,800 --> 00:39:13,840
I also brought you
some famous Yaowarat guay jub.

461
00:39:21,000 --> 00:39:21,840
Come in.

462
00:39:36,680 --> 00:39:39,720
When I dropped you off last time,
I noticed there wasn't much to eat nearby,

463
00:39:40,320 --> 00:39:41,520
so I brought you something.

464
00:39:52,720 --> 00:39:55,560
You should've called me first.

465
00:39:58,760 --> 00:40:00,720
Are you uncomfortable with me coming here?

466
00:40:02,600 --> 00:40:05,760
No. I was just worried
you'd come and I wouldn't be here.

467
00:40:07,200 --> 00:40:10,880
If I went out for food,
you'd be outside feeding mosquitoes.

468
00:40:14,160 --> 00:40:17,280
I'd stand outside feeding mosquitoes
just to see you.

469
00:40:31,280 --> 00:40:32,360
Fon.

470
00:40:33,160 --> 00:40:36,000
Uh, I'm hungry.

471
00:40:37,120 --> 00:40:38,040
Let's eat.

472
00:41:03,600 --> 00:41:05,520
I still love you the same, Fon.

473
00:41:13,360 --> 00:41:14,560
- Will you go out with--
- Oab.

474
00:41:16,840 --> 00:41:19,040
We haven't seen each other for years.

475
00:41:19,720 --> 00:41:22,240
I might not be the person
you used to love anymore.

476
00:41:23,720 --> 00:41:25,880
Before you tell me you love me,

477
00:41:25,960 --> 00:41:28,760
shouldn't we get to know each other again?

478
00:41:30,400 --> 00:41:31,720
If you get to know who I am now,

479
00:41:33,000 --> 00:41:34,720
you might not like me anymore.

480
00:41:42,600 --> 00:41:45,840
Whether it's today or ten years from now,

481
00:41:47,800 --> 00:41:50,080
I'll still love you the same.

482
00:41:56,400 --> 00:41:57,440
But…

483
00:41:58,240 --> 00:42:00,320
if you want
to get to know who I am now better,

484
00:42:03,320 --> 00:42:04,520
I'll give you time.

485
00:42:09,440 --> 00:42:10,440
Okay.

486
00:43:46,040 --> 00:43:46,960
Is he gone?

487
00:43:51,280 --> 00:43:52,440
You and Oab used to date?

488
00:44:02,680 --> 00:44:03,560
Yes.

489
00:44:06,600 --> 00:44:08,280
Do you still like him?

490
00:44:09,960 --> 00:44:11,040
No.

491
00:44:17,200 --> 00:44:20,320
But taking this case
means you'll be with him again, right?

492
00:44:26,400 --> 00:44:28,480
I don't want you involved in this case.

493
00:44:30,280 --> 00:44:32,040
Because Oab and I used to be together?

494
00:44:32,680 --> 00:44:33,880
Yes.

495
00:44:35,760 --> 00:44:36,800
Dom.

496
00:44:41,560 --> 00:44:43,640
You don't trust me anymore?

497
00:44:44,360 --> 00:44:47,520
I do. But I don't trust him.

498
00:44:48,440 --> 00:44:50,720
And I don't want you being close to him.

499
00:44:56,320 --> 00:44:59,000
Fon, is there really no other way?

500
00:44:59,800 --> 00:45:03,280
Anything that doesn't require you
to do this? Please.

501
00:45:05,520 --> 00:45:07,280
There's no other way.

502
00:45:08,240 --> 00:45:10,320
If there was,
they wouldn't have sent you in there.

503
00:45:18,680 --> 00:45:20,680
I'm afraid you'll change your mind

504
00:45:22,280 --> 00:45:24,000
and fall in love with him again.

505
00:45:33,720 --> 00:45:35,440
I'll never change.

506
00:45:43,440 --> 00:45:45,080
I won't change my feelings.

507
00:46:24,720 --> 00:46:25,640
You're still awake?

508
00:46:30,960 --> 00:46:32,680
You left since this evening

509
00:46:32,760 --> 00:46:34,840
and didn't tell me where you were going.

510
00:46:34,920 --> 00:46:37,400
You just said it was personal business.

511
00:46:37,480 --> 00:46:40,880
Then you wouldn't let me come with you.
You think I could sleep?

512
00:46:45,800 --> 00:46:46,840
Where did you go?

513
00:46:47,720 --> 00:46:50,520
Why? Why do you need to know?

514
00:46:52,200 --> 00:46:53,160
Fine, don't tell me.

515
00:46:54,840 --> 00:46:56,400
Now that you're back, I can go to sleep.

516
00:46:57,720 --> 00:46:59,240
I went to see Fon.

517
00:47:07,840 --> 00:47:09,120
I know you don't agree,

518
00:47:11,120 --> 00:47:12,880
but I want you to know

519
00:47:13,880 --> 00:47:15,280
that I'm trying to win her over.

520
00:47:16,760 --> 00:47:18,560
If she's okay with it,

521
00:47:18,640 --> 00:47:20,520
I'm going to date her.

522
00:47:20,600 --> 00:47:24,400
How many times do I have to tell you?
Fon is a cop.

523
00:47:25,040 --> 00:47:26,000
So what?

524
00:47:27,200 --> 00:47:28,440
I can't date her?

525
00:47:29,160 --> 00:47:32,560
How can you say that? I understand.

526
00:47:33,080 --> 00:47:35,240
You can't control feelings like this.

527
00:47:35,320 --> 00:47:36,560
- Yeah.
- But what I don't like

528
00:47:36,640 --> 00:47:40,040
is you! You're not being careful at all.

529
00:47:40,120 --> 00:47:43,120
She's a cop, you know. She's a cop!

530
00:47:44,920 --> 00:47:47,480
And knowing that doesn't stop you.

531
00:47:47,560 --> 00:47:50,240
At least check her background.

532
00:47:50,320 --> 00:47:52,800
Find out who she is, her background,
and if she'll cause trouble.

533
00:47:52,880 --> 00:47:53,960
Why bother checking?

534
00:47:54,040 --> 00:47:57,280
I know her parents.
I've known Fon since she was a kid.

535
00:47:57,360 --> 00:47:59,680
- Isn't that enough?
- But you haven't seen her for years.

536
00:48:00,520 --> 00:48:03,080
Right?
How do you know she's still the same?

537
00:48:03,160 --> 00:48:06,120
How do you know she still means well?

538
00:48:11,360 --> 00:48:12,800
You told me not to get involved.

539
00:48:14,840 --> 00:48:16,080
Honestly, I can't ignore this.

540
00:48:16,840 --> 00:48:18,800
At least let me check her background.

541
00:48:21,720 --> 00:48:23,640
If she really is as good as you say,

542
00:48:25,080 --> 00:48:26,600
I won't have a problem
with you dating her.

543
00:48:45,000 --> 00:48:46,360
Really?

544
00:48:46,440 --> 00:48:48,960
She was a markswoman in Ban Haet,

545
00:48:49,040 --> 00:48:50,520
just transferred
to the Crime Suppression Division,

546
00:48:50,600 --> 00:48:52,000
and she's single too.

547
00:48:52,080 --> 00:48:54,480
She hasn't handled any cases
involving influential figures.

548
00:48:55,600 --> 00:48:58,680
Yeah, that's all the report has.
That's pretty much all there is.

549
00:48:59,760 --> 00:49:00,640
I don't see anything suspicious.

550
00:49:02,440 --> 00:49:05,440
- Well?
- I don't know what his deal is.

551
00:49:05,520 --> 00:49:06,840
I don't know why he's so suspicious.

552
00:49:08,200 --> 00:49:11,480
I told you Fon could be trusted.
You just didn't believe me.

553
00:49:13,200 --> 00:49:14,160
Yeah.

554
00:49:16,840 --> 00:49:18,320
I guess I was just overthinking it.

555
00:49:19,160 --> 00:49:20,920
But there's nothing wrong
with being careful.

556
00:49:22,280 --> 00:49:23,320
You were worried about me.

557
00:49:23,920 --> 00:49:24,840
I know.

558
00:49:27,760 --> 00:49:29,520
Now you can stop suspecting Fon.

559
00:49:39,160 --> 00:49:41,560
It's not easy for Oab
to fall in love with someone, Pong.

560
00:49:42,280 --> 00:49:43,560
Don't stand in his way.

561
00:49:44,680 --> 00:49:45,520
Yeah.

562
00:49:46,560 --> 00:49:48,960
You two really are in sync.

563
00:49:54,400 --> 00:49:55,640
Pong.

564
00:49:55,720 --> 00:49:57,640
What are you two planning to do?

565
00:49:58,640 --> 00:49:59,480
What do you mean?

566
00:50:00,640 --> 00:50:04,440
I got word from one of my sources.
Are you guys planning to go after Peng?

567
00:50:06,800 --> 00:50:07,920
You know a lot, don't you?

568
00:50:09,040 --> 00:50:11,040
If word got to me,
it can get to others too.

569
00:50:13,560 --> 00:50:15,360
You need to be more careful.

570
00:50:22,000 --> 00:50:23,040
Thanks.

571
00:50:25,120 --> 00:50:26,440
Good luck, friend.

572
00:50:36,240 --> 00:50:38,360
Pom said there's a rumor
that we're after Peng.

573
00:50:41,240 --> 00:50:43,600
That means he probably knows by now.

574
00:50:46,480 --> 00:50:48,920
Then set up a meeting
with the landowner. Tonight.

575
00:50:49,800 --> 00:50:53,160
Tell him if he won't accept my offer,
I don't want the land anymore.

576
00:50:53,240 --> 00:50:55,320
But you really want that land, don't you?

577
00:50:57,320 --> 00:50:58,320
I do.

578
00:50:59,480 --> 00:51:02,800
But I don't think Peng will pay more.
Trust me.

579
00:51:04,360 --> 00:51:06,080
He'll end up selling it to me.

580
00:51:13,800 --> 00:51:15,240
- Champ.
- Huh?

581
00:51:16,800 --> 00:51:18,360
Have you seen this case before?

582
00:51:19,040 --> 00:51:19,880
Which case?

583
00:51:19,960 --> 00:51:23,160
The case where two suspects
were shot by police near the border.

584
00:51:27,120 --> 00:51:28,120
Why?

585
00:51:28,720 --> 00:51:30,760
They surrendered.

586
00:51:30,840 --> 00:51:32,840
Do you think the police
used excessive force?

587
00:51:35,440 --> 00:51:37,520
Let me see.

588
00:51:37,600 --> 00:51:39,440
Here, this one.

589
00:51:44,000 --> 00:51:46,240
It says here that during the reenactment,

590
00:51:46,320 --> 00:51:48,440
the two suspects pulled out hidden guns,

591
00:51:48,520 --> 00:51:50,480
forcing the police to shoot them.

592
00:51:52,960 --> 00:51:54,840
But it happened inside a house.

593
00:51:54,920 --> 00:51:57,160
No one witnessed what happened.

594
00:51:59,600 --> 00:52:01,040
What are you suspecting?

595
00:52:01,120 --> 00:52:04,080
I'm wondering
if the suspects killed by police

596
00:52:04,160 --> 00:52:06,120
could have been the hitmen
from Arm's case.

597
00:52:06,760 --> 00:52:07,960
Look at this.

598
00:52:09,400 --> 00:52:13,160
From their previous cases,

599
00:52:13,760 --> 00:52:15,760
there was nothing related to drugs at all,

600
00:52:16,280 --> 00:52:18,080
except for a murder-for-hire case.

601
00:52:18,160 --> 00:52:20,880
So was this really a justified shooting

602
00:52:20,960 --> 00:52:23,040
or were they silenced?

603
00:52:47,360 --> 00:52:48,920
- Dom.
- Huh?

604
00:52:49,760 --> 00:52:51,760
You've only just recovered.
Take it easy, man.

605
00:52:51,840 --> 00:52:53,080
I am.

606
00:52:53,160 --> 00:52:54,760
The hell you are.

607
00:52:56,440 --> 00:52:58,120
I can barely catch my breath.

608
00:52:59,360 --> 00:53:00,360
Where do you get that energy?

609
00:53:04,920 --> 00:53:06,560
- I'm gonna go shower.
- Yeah.

610
00:53:06,640 --> 00:53:07,760
I can't do this anymore.

611
00:53:07,840 --> 00:53:08,840
Yeah.

612
00:53:09,560 --> 00:53:11,360
I'm showering, then I'm going to bed.
I'm not waiting.

613
00:53:11,440 --> 00:53:12,480
Yeah.

614
00:53:12,560 --> 00:53:14,280
Put my gloves away for me. I'm done.

615
00:53:36,680 --> 00:53:37,840
You sure you can train?

616
00:53:39,080 --> 00:53:40,320
I can, Oab.

617
00:53:43,920 --> 00:53:45,880
If you want me to keep doing this,

618
00:53:46,720 --> 00:53:47,880
I have to give it my all.

619
00:53:49,120 --> 00:53:52,600
If you send me back there to fight again,
I don't want to lose.

620
00:53:55,400 --> 00:53:58,200
Anyway, about the liquor.
Pong has taken care of it.

621
00:53:59,000 --> 00:54:01,920
Good. At least you won't need
those imported liquor suppliers anymore.

622
00:54:03,720 --> 00:54:05,040
We'll have to wait and see.

623
00:54:06,160 --> 00:54:08,680
- You're done training, right?
- Yes.

624
00:54:08,760 --> 00:54:10,920
Go take a shower, then come with me.

625
00:54:20,160 --> 00:54:21,520
The same thing again?

626
00:54:32,840 --> 00:54:33,680
Thanks.

627
00:54:33,760 --> 00:54:34,720
Yeah.

628
00:54:35,320 --> 00:54:37,840
You've been looking into
this case for days. Found anything?

629
00:54:43,120 --> 00:54:46,080
I can show it to you,
but I think you should stay out of it.

630
00:54:46,880 --> 00:54:48,760
- Why?
- If this case is still unsolved,

631
00:54:48,840 --> 00:54:50,040
there has to be a reason.

632
00:54:50,640 --> 00:54:53,440
The investigators aren't
the only people who know about it.

633
00:54:53,520 --> 00:54:55,920
Whoever approved
hiding the investigators' names

634
00:54:56,000 --> 00:54:57,680
must be someone high up.

635
00:55:03,560 --> 00:55:06,560
You just transferred here.
Don't get yourself into trouble.

636
00:55:34,640 --> 00:55:35,600
Wow.

637
00:55:36,400 --> 00:55:39,120
That's a lot of money.
What are you going to do with it?

638
00:55:39,880 --> 00:55:41,040
Buy land.

639
00:55:41,720 --> 00:55:44,600
With this much money,
the land must be huge.

640
00:55:44,680 --> 00:55:46,040
Yeah.

641
00:55:47,200 --> 00:55:48,440
Drive for me, will you?

642
00:55:48,520 --> 00:55:52,000
Sure. What about Pong? Isn't he coming?

643
00:55:52,960 --> 00:55:54,240
I told him to wait there.

644
00:57:16,960 --> 00:57:17,920
That's all you brought?

645
00:57:18,520 --> 00:57:19,360
Is Oab in the car?

646
00:57:19,440 --> 00:57:21,280
Want to know where he went?

647
00:57:22,160 --> 00:57:23,920
He's meeting your boss.

648
00:57:32,760 --> 00:57:33,880
You're taking Fon with you?

649
00:57:33,960 --> 00:57:35,240
Where are we going?

650
00:57:36,520 --> 00:57:37,240
Khon Kaen.

651
00:57:38,480 --> 00:57:39,960
- Is that you, Oab?
- Hello, Dad.

652
00:57:40,040 --> 00:57:41,080
Hello.

653
00:57:41,160 --> 00:57:43,040
Who drove you here?

654
00:57:46,200 --> 00:57:47,920
Why don't you get out of the car?

655
00:57:48,000 --> 00:57:48,920
Come on.

656
00:57:49,000 --> 00:57:51,320
It must be hot in there.

657
00:58:36,000 --> 00:58:37,680
Subtitle translation by:
Chomchanach Yanaharn
